  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the western districts of Toulon, near the Pont du Las, the Parc des Cèdres is a neighbourhood park at 313 rue Félix Mayol. The city of Toulon lists it among its dog areas, green spaces where dogs can move around freely, according to the city.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park is in the list of dog areas in the municipal document "Toulon, ville amie des chiens" (published online in November 2025). The document reminds visitors that a leash is compulsory throughout the municipality and that picking up waste is compulsory everywhere, including inside the dog parks. More than 300 bag dispensers are spread across the municipality, and waste left behind can bring a class 4 fine (€135). The park page on toulon.fr gives opening daily, 9am to 7pm.</p>
      <p>Dogs must be identified, as everywhere in France; the city points to the i-cad register. For any question about dogs in town, the town hall's Service Animal en Ville answers on 04 94 36 30 26.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: a neighbourhood spot for a green break, with no need to plan a whole afternoon.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The western districts of Toulon and the Pont du Las area are right next door, handy for fitting this break into an urban walk. For more room to run, the municipal list names other dog areas (parc de la Florane, parc Raoulx, jardin Alexandre 1er, parc des Lices with an agility zone, parc des plages du Mourillon). The Sentier des douaniers and the chemin de la Mitre are open to dogs on a leash from 1 October to 30 April, and the Faron massif also welcomes dogs, which ride the cable car free according to the city.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> the size and equipment of the dog area are not published by the city.</p>
    </div>

